# Directories
out/
vcpkg_installed/

# Visual Studio's per-user scratch state -- databases, indexes, window layout.
#
# `.vs/*` RATHER THAN `.vs/`, and the difference is the only reason the line
# below works: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded,
# so `.vs/` would make the negation silently inert. Excluding the contents
# instead leaves the directory itself visible and the exception effective.
#
# The one exception is workspace configuration rather than user state: it says
# which files Visual Studio should not scan, and the answer is the same for
# everybody who clones this (see the header comment inside it).
.vs/*
!.vs/VSWorkspaceSettings.json

# Files
CMakeSettings.json
# Visual Studio resource-editor intermediate (binary, regenerated from app.rc)
*.aps

# Python bytecode. scripts/check_determinism_flags.py grew an importable
# helper and running it now leaves a __pycache__ beside the sources.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# CTest scratch (Testing/Temporary). Written by any ctest run in the source
# tree; never an input to anything.
Testing/

# The editor's Build action writes bundles here (BuildSettings default output).
# It is build OUTPUT: a player exe, every runtime DLL, and a copy of the whole
# Exported/ tree. `git add -A` swept 67 of those files into a commit once.
Builds/
